 5| ## Responsibility
 6| 
 7| `Ring<T>` is a fixed-capacity ring buffer implementing FIFO
 8| (first-in, first-out) semantics over a circular backing array.
 9| 
10| ## Contract
11| 
12| - `constructor(capacity)` — requires a positive integer capacity;
13|   throws `RangeError` otherwise.
14| - `enqueue(item)` — appends at the tail; throws on overflow (full).
15| - `dequeue()` — removes and returns the oldest item; throws on
16|   underflow (empty).
17| - `peek()` — returns the oldest item without removing it; throws on
18|   underflow.
19| - `size` — current number of stored items (read-only).
20| 
21| ## Invariants
22| 
23| - `0 <= size <= capacity` at all times.
24| - Dequeue order exactly matches enqueue order (strict FIFO).
25| - All operations are O(1); the backing array never grows or shifts.
26| - Vacated slots are cleared, so no stale references are retained.
27| - Capacity is immutable after construction.

